{
  "title": "51: al-Zaareyaat الذاريات",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nوَالذّٰرِيٰتِ ذَرْوًا ۙ‏(1)\nWAALZZAAREETE ZARWAN.\nBy the (Winds) that scatter broadcast; \nفَالْحٰمِلٰتِ وِقْرًا ۙ‏(2)\nFAL HAAMELAATE WEQRAN.\nAnd those that lift and bear away heavy weights; \nفَالْجٰرِيٰتِ يُسْرًا ۙ‏(3)\nFAL JAAREETE YUSRAN.\nAnd those that flow with ease and gentleness; \nفَالْمُقَسِّمٰتِ اَمْرًا ۙ‏(4)\nFAL MUQASSEMAATE AMRAN.\nAnd those that distribute and apportion by Command;- \nاِنَّمَا تُوْعَدُوْنَ لَصَادِقٌ ۙ‏(5)\nINNAMAA TOO-A’DOON LASAADEQUN.\nVerily that which ye are promised is true; \nوَّاِنَّ الدِّيْنَ لوَاقِعٌ ؕ‏(6)\nWWAANNA DEENA LWAAQEA’UN.\nAnd verily Judgment and Justice must indeed come to pass. \nوَالسَّمَآءِ ذَاتِ الْحُبُكِ ۙ‏(7)\nWAS SAMAAA-E ZAATIL AL-HUBUKE.\nBy the Sky with (its) numerous Paths, \nاِنَّكُمْ لَفِىْ قَوْلٍ مُّخْتَلِفٍ ۙ‏(8)\nINNAKUM LAFEE QAWLIN MMUKHTALEFIN.\nTruly ye are in a doctrine discordant, \nيُّؤْفَكُ عَنْهُ مَنْ اُفِكَ ؕ‏(9)\nYYUFAKU A’NHO MAN AUFEKA.\nThrough which are deluded (away from the Truth) such as would be deluded. \nقُتِلَ الْخَرّٰصُوْنَۙ‏(10)\nQOTELAL AL-KHARRAASOONA.\nWoe to the falsehood-mongers, \nالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ فِىْ غَمْرَةٍ سَاهُوْنَۙ‏(11)\nLAZEENA HUM FEE GHAMRATIN SAAHOONAL.\nThose who (flounder) heedless in a flood of confusion: \nيَسْئَلُوْنَ اَيَّانَ يَوْمُ الدِّيْنِؕ‏(12)\nYAS-ALOONAN AYYAANA YAWMUD DEEN.\nThey ask, “When will be the Day of Judgment and Justice?” \nيَوْمَ هُمْ عَلَى النَّارِ يُفْتَنُوْنَ‏(13)\nYAWMA HUM A’LAL NAAR LAA YUFTANOON.\n(It will be) a Day when they will be tried (and tested) over the Fire! \nذُوْقُوْا فِتْنَتَكُمْؕ هٰذَا الَّذِىْ كُنْتُمْ بِهٖ تَسْتَعْجِلُوْنَ‏(14)\nZOOQOO FETNATAKUM HAAZAL LAZEE KUNTUM BEHI TAS-TA’JELOONA.\n“Taste ye your trial! This is what ye used to ask to be hastened!” \nاِنَّ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ فِىْ جَنّٰتٍ وَّعُيُوْنٍۙ‏(15)\nINNAL MA-A’L MUTTAQEEN FEE JANNAATIN WA O’OYOONINW.\nAs to the Righteous, they will be in the midst of Gardens and Springs, \nاٰخِذِيْنَ مَاۤ اٰتٰٮهُمْ رَبُّهُمْ‌ؕ اِنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا قَبْلَ ذٰلِكَ مُحْسِنِيْنَؕ‏(16)\nAAAKHEZEENA MAA AAATAAHUM RABBUHUM INNAHUM KAANOO QABLA ZAALEKA MUHSENEENA.\nTaking joy in the things which their Lord gives them, because, before then, they lived a good life. \nكَانُوْا قَلِيْلًا مِّنَ الَّيْلِ مَا يَهْجَعُوْنَ‏(17)\nKAANOO QALEELAA MENAL LAYLE MAA YAHJAU’OONA.\nThey were in the habit of sleeping but little by night, \nوَبِالْاَسْحَارِ هُمْ يَسْتَغْفِرُوْنَ‏(18)\nWABEALAASHAARE HUM YASTAGHFEROONA.\nAnd in the hour of early dawn, they (were found) praying for Forgiveness; \nوَفِىْۤ اَمْوَالِهِمْ حَقٌّ لِّلسَّآئِلِ وَالْمَحْرُوْمِ‏(19)\nWA FEE AAMWAALEHEM HAQQUWN LLELSSAAELE WAL MAHROOME.\nAnd in their wealth and possessions (was remembered) the right of the (needy,) him who asked, and him who (for some reason) was prevented (from asking). \nوَفِى الْاَرْضِ اٰيٰتٌ لِّلْمُوْقِنِيْنَۙ‏(20)\nWA ARZE AAYAATUM LLELMOOQENEENA.\nOn the earth are signs for those of assured Faith, \nوَفِىْۤ اَنْفُسِكُمْ‌ؕ اَفَلَا تُبْصِرُوْنَ‏(21)\nWA FEE ANFOSEKUM AFALAA TUBSEROON.\nAs also in your own selves: Will ye not then see? \nوَفِى السَّمَآءِ رِزْقُكُمْ وَمَا تُوْعَدُوْنَ‏(22)\nWA SAMAAA-E REZQUKUM WA MAA TOO-A’DOON.\nAnd in heaven is your Sustenance, as (also) that which ye are promised. \nفَوَرَبِّ السَّمَآءِ وَالْاَرْضِ اِنَّهٗ لَحَقٌّ مِّثْلَ مَاۤ اَنَّكُمْ تَنْطِقُوْنَ‏(23)\nFAWARABBE SAMAAA-E WAL ARZE INNAHU LAHAQQUN MISLA MAA ANNAKUM TANTEQOONA.\nThen, by the Lord of heaven and earth, this is the very Truth, as much as the fact that ye can speak intelligently to each other. \nهَلْ اَتٰٮكَ حَدِيْثُ ضَيْفِ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ الْمُكْرَمِيْنَ‌ۘ‏(24)\nHAL ATAAKA HADEESUL ZAYFE IBRAAHEEMA MUKRAMEEN.\nHas the story reached thee, of the honoured guests of Abraham? \nاِذْ دَخَلُوْا عَلَيْهِ فَقَالُوْا سَلٰمًا‌ؕ قَالَ سَلٰمٌ ۚ قَوْمٌ مُّنْكَرُوْنَ‌‏(25)\nIZ DAKHALOO A’LAYHE FA-QAALOO SALAAMAN QAALA SALAAMUN QAWMUN MMUNKAROONA.\nBehold, they entered his presence, and said: “Peace!” He said, “Peace!” (and thought, “These seem) unusual people.” \nفَرَاغَ اِلٰٓى اَهْلِهٖ فَجَآءَ بِعِجْلٍ سَمِيْنٍۙ‏(26)\nFARAAGHA ELAA AHLEHI FA JAAA-A BEE’EJLIN SAMEENIN.\nThen he turned quickly to his household, brought out a fatted calf, \nفَقَرَّبَهٗۤ اِلَيْهِمْ قَالَ اَلَا تَاْكُلُوْنَ‏(27)\nFAQARRABAH ELAYHIM QAALAL ALAA TAAKULOONA.\nAnd placed it before them.. he said, “Will ye not eat?” \nفَاَوْجَسَ مِنْهُمْ خِيْفَةً‌ؕ قَالُوْا لَا تَخَفْ‌ ؕ وَبَشَّرُوْهُ بِغُلٰمٍ عَلِيْمٍ‏(28)\nFAAWJASA MINHUM KHEEFATAN QAALOO LAA TAKHAF WABASSHAROOHU BEGHULAAMIN A’LEEM.\n(When they did not eat), He conceived a fear of them. They said, “Fear not,” and they gave him glad tidings of a son endowed with knowledge. \nفَاَقْبَلَتِ امْرَاَتُهٗ فِىْ صَرَّةٍ فَصَكَّتْ وَجْهَهَا وَقَالَتْ عَجُوْزٌ عَقِيْمٌ‏(29)\nFAAQBALATE AMRAATUH FEE SARRATIN FASAKKAT WAJHAHAA WA QAALAT A’AJOOZUN A’AQEEMUN.\nBut his wife came forward (laughing) aloud: she smote her forehead and said: “A barren old woman!” \nقَالُوْا كَذٰلِكِ ۙ قَالَ رَبُّكِ‌ؕ اِنَّهٗ هُوَ الْحَكِيْمُ الْعَلِيْمُ‏(30)\nQAALOO KAZAALEKE QAALA RABBUKE INNAHU HOWA HAKEEM A’LEEM.\nThey said, “Even so has thy Lord spoken: and He is full of Wisdom and Knowledge.” \nقَالَ فَمَا خَطْبُكُمْ اَيُّهَا الْمُرْسَلُوْنَ‏(31)\nQAALA FAMAA KHATBUKUM AYYOHAL MURSALOON.\n(Abraham) said: “And what, O ye Messengers, is your errand (now)?” \nقَالُوْۤا اِنَّاۤ اُرْسِلْنَاۤ اِلٰى قَوْمٍ مُّجْرِمِيْنَۙ‏(32)\nQAALOO INNAA AURSELNAA ELAA QAWMIN MMUJREMEENA.\nThey said, “We have been sent to a people (deep) in sin;- \nلِنُرْسِلَ عَلَيْهِمْ حِجَارَةً مِّنْ طِيْنٍۙ‏(33)\nLENURSELA A’LAYHIM HEJAARATAN MIN TEENIN.\n“To bring on, on them, (a shower of) stones of clay (brimstone), \nمُّسَوَّمَةً عِنْدَ رَبِّكَ لِلْمُسْرِفِيْنَ‏(34)\nMMUSAWMATAN I’NDAL RABBEKA LIL-MUSREFEENA.\n“Marked as from thy Lord for those who trespass beyond bounds.” \nفَاَخْرَجْنَا مَنْ كَانَ فِيْهَا مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(35)\nFA AKH-RAJNAA MAN KAANA FEEHAA MENAL MOAMENEEN.\nThen We evacuated those of the Believers who were there, \nفَمَا وَجَدْنَا فِيْهَا غَيْرَ بَيْتٍ مِّنَ الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(36)\nFAMAA WAJADNAA FEEHAA GHAYRA BAYTIYN MENAL AKOONA MENAL MUSLEMEEN.\nBut We found not there any just (Muslim) persons except in one house: \nوَتَرَكْنَا فِيْهَاۤ اٰيَةً لِّلَّذِيْنَ يَخَافُوْنَ الْعَذَابَ الْاَلِيْمَؕ‏(37)\nWATARAKNAA FEEHAA AAYATAL LIL-LAZEENA YAKHAAFOONA A’ZAABA AL-AALEEMA.\nAnd We left there a Sign for such as fear the Grievous Penalty. \nوَفِىْ مُوْسٰۤی اِذْ اَرْسَلْنٰهُ اِلٰى فِرْعَوْنَ بِسُلْطٰنٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(38)\nWA FEE MOOSAAY IZ AARSALNAAHU ELAA FIR-A’WNA BESULTAANIM MOBEEN.\nAnd in Moses (was another Sign): Behold, We sent him to Pharaoh, with authority manifest. \nفَتَوَلّٰى بِرُكْنِهٖ وَقَالَ سٰحِرٌ اَوْ مَجْنُوْنٌ‏(39)\nFA TAWALLAA BERUKNEH WA QAALA SAAHERUN AW MAJNOONUN.\nBut (Pharaoh) turned back with his Chiefs, and said, “A sorcerer, or one possessed!” \nفَاَخَذْنٰهُ وَجُنُوْدَهٗ فَنَبَذْنٰهُمْ فِى الْيَمِّ وَهُوَ مُلِيْمٌؕ‏(40)\nFA-AKHAZNAAHO WA JONOODOHU FANABAZNAAHUM FIL WA WA HOWA MULEEMUN.\nSo We took him and his forces, and threw them into the sea; and his was the blame. \nوَفِىْ عَادٍ اِذْ اَرْسَلْنَا عَلَيْهِمُ الرِّيْحَ الْعَقِيْمَ‌ۚ‏(41)\nWA FEE A’ADIN IZ ARSALNAA A’LAYHEMUL AR-REEHA AL-A’AQEEMA.\nAnd in the 'Ad (people) (was another Sign): Behold, We sent against them the devastating Wind: \nمَا تَذَرُ مِنْ شَىْءٍ اَتَتْ عَلَيْهِ اِلَّا جَعَلَتْهُ كَالرَّمِيْمِؕ‏(42)\nMAA TAZARU MIN SHAY-IN AATAT A’LAYHE ILLAA JAA’ALATHU KAALRRAMEEME.\nIt left nothing whatever that it came up against, but reduced it to ruin and rottenness. \nوَفِىْ ثَمُوْدَ اِذْ قِيْلَ لَهُمْ تَمَتَّعُوْا حَتّٰى حِيْنٍ‏(43)\nWA FEE ELAA IZ QEELA LAHUM TAMATTAU’OOA HATTAA HEEN.\nAnd in the Thamud (was another Sign): Behold, they were told, “Enjoy (your brief day) for a little while!” \nفَعَتَوْا عَنْ اَمْرِ رَبِّهِمْ فَاَخَذَتْهُمُ الصّٰعِقَةُ وَ هُمْ يَنْظُرُوْنَ‏(44)\nFAA’ATAWA A’N AMRE RABBEHIM FA-AKHAZATHOMUR SAA-E’QATO WA HUM YANZOROONA.\nBut they insolently defied the Command of their Lord: So the stunning noise (of an earthquake) seized them, even while they were looking on. \nفَمَا اسْتَطَاعُوْا مِنْ قِيَامٍ وَّمَا كَانُوْا مُنْتَصِرِيْنَۙ‏(45)\nFAMAA TATAA-O’O MIN QEEAMIN WA MAA KAANOO MUNTASEREENA.\nThen they could not even stand (on their feet), nor could they help themselves. \nوَقَوْمَ نُوْحٍ مِّنْ قَبْلُ‌ؕ اِنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا قَوْمًا فٰسِقِيْنَ‏(46)\nWA QAWMA NOOHIN MIN QABL WA INNAHUM KAANOO QAWMAN FAASEQEEN.\nSo were the People of Noah before them for they wickedly transgressed. \nوَ السَّمَآءَ بَنَيْنٰهَا بِاَيْٮدٍ وَّاِنَّا لَمُوْسِعُوْنَ‏(47)\nWAL SAMAAA-AD BANAYNAAHAA BEAAYDIN WWAANNAA LAMOOSEU’OONA.\nWith power and skill did We construct the Firmament: for it is We Who create the vastness of pace. \nوَالْاَرْضَ فَرَشْنٰهَا فَنِعْمَ الْمٰهِدُوْنَ‏(48)\nWAL ARZA FARASHNAAHAA FA NE’MA AL-MAAHEDOONA.\nAnd We have spread out the (spacious) earth: How excellently We do spread out! \nوَمِنْ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ خَلَقْنَا زَوْجَيْنِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَذَكَّرُوْنَ‏(49)\nWA MIN KULLE SHAY-IN KHALAQNAL ZAWJAYNE LA-A’LLAKUM TAZAKKAROON.\nAnd of every thing We have created pairs: That ye may receive instruction. \nفَفِرُّوْۤا اِلَى اللّٰهِ‌ؕ اِنِّىْ لَكُمْ مِّنْهُ نَذِيْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌ‌ۚ‏(50)\nFAFERROOA ELAL LAAH INNEE LAKUM MINHO NAZEERUM MOBEEN.\nHasten ye then (at once) to Allah: I am from Him a Warner to you, clear and open! \nوَلَا تَجْعَلُوْا مَعَ اللّٰهِ اِلٰهًا اٰخَرَ‌ؕ اِنِّىْ لَكُمْ مِّنْهُ نَذِيْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌ‌ۚ‏(51)\nWA LAA TAJ-A’LOO LAAHA LAAHE ELAAHANW AAAKHARA INNEE LAKUM MINHO NAZEERUM MOBEEN.\nAnd make not another an object of worship with Allah: I am from Him a Warner to you, clear and open! \nكَذٰلِكَ مَاۤ اَتَى الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ مِّنْ رَّسُوْلٍ اِلَّا قَالُوْا سَاحِرٌ اَوْ مَجْنُوْنٌ‌ۚ‏(52)\nKAZAALEKA MAA AATAA LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM MIR RASOOLIN ILLAA QAALOO SAAHERUN AW MAJNOONUN.\nSimilarly, no messenger came to the Peoples before them, but they said (of him) in like manner, “A sorcerer, or one possessed”! \nاَتَوَاصَوْا بِهٖ‌ۚ بَلْ هُمْ قَوْمٌ طَاغُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(53)\nAATAWAASAWA BEHI BAL HUM QAWMUN TAAGHOONA.\nIs this the legacy they have transmitted, one to another? Nay, they are themselves a people transgressing beyond bounds! \nفَتَوَلَّ عَنْهُمْ فَمَاۤ اَنْتَ بِمَلُوْمٍ‏(54)\nFA TAWALLA A’NHUM FAMAA ANTA BEMALOOMIN.\nSo turn away from them: not thine is the blame. \nوَّذَكِّرْ فَاِنَّ الذِّكْرٰى تَنْفَعُ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(55)\nWWAZAKKER FA-INNAL ZIKRAA TANFAU’U MOAMENEEN.\nBut teach (thy Message) for teaching benefits the Believers. \nوَمَا خَلَقْتُ الْجِنَّ وَالْاِنْسَ اِلَّا لِيَعْبُدُوْنِ‏(56)\nWA MAA KHALAQTU AL-JENNA WAL AENSA ILLAA LEEA’BUDOONE.\nI have only created Jinns and men, that they may serve Me. \nمَاۤ اُرِيْدُ مِنْهُمْ مِّنْ رِّزْقٍ وَّمَاۤ اُرِيْدُ اَنْ يُّطْعِمُوْنِ‏(57)\nMAA OREEDO MINHUM MIR RREZQIN WA MAA OREEDO AN YYUTE’EMOONE.\nNo Sustenance do I require of them, nor do I require that they should feed Me. \nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ هُوَ الرَّزَّاقُ ذُو الْقُوَّةِ الْمَتِيْنُ‏(58)\nINNAL LAAHA HOWA AR-RAZZAAQU ZUL QUWWAH AL-MATEENU.\nFor Allah is He Who gives (all) Sustenance, Lord of Power, Steadfast (for ever). \nفَاِنَّ لِلَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا ذَنُوْبًا مِّثْلَ ذَنُوْبِ اَصْحٰبِهِمْ فَلَا يَسْتَعْجِلُوْنِ‏(59)\nFA-INNAL LILLAZEENA ZALAMOO ZANOOBAN MISLA ZANOOBE AASHAABEHEM FALAA YASTAA’JELOONE.\nFor the Wrong-doers, their portion is like unto the portion of their fellows (of earlier generations): then let them not ask Me to hasten (that portion)! \nفَوَيْلٌ لِّلَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا مِنْ يَّوْمِهِمُ الَّذِىْ يُوْعَدُوْنَ‏(60)\nLAHUM LIL-LAZEENA KAFAROO MIN YYAWMEHEMU LAZEE YOOA’ADOONA.\nWoe, then, to the Unbelievers, on account of that Day of theirs which they have been promised!",
  "merits": "Surah al-Zaareyaat (The Scatterers)\nThere are 60 verses in this Surah and it was revealed in Makkah. In the commentary of Majma’ul Bayan it is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that the reward for reciting this Surah is ten times the number of moving winds or breezes.\nImam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that recitation of this Surah increases ones sustenance and makes it easy to earn. Drinking water in which this Surah was dissolved after being written acts as a remedy for back problems (e.g. backaches). If a pregnant woman wears a talisman of Surah al-Zaareyaat, her pregnancy and delivery will be easy. Keeping this Surah close to a dying person makes his death easy."
}
